By lovable:
Next-week plan independence + Monday pantry reconcile

Problem

Today, "This week" and "Next week" plans both consume the same inventory list as pantryItems when calling generate-ma-semaine (see src/pages/MaSemaine.tsx ~L887 and again at L971/L1056/L1145). Because the AI is heavily steered by the pantry ("URGENT — prioritize these expiring pantry items…", pantryMatch, expiring-hero rule in supabase/functions/generate-ma-semaine/index.ts), next week ends up echoing this week.

We will (1) treat the pantry as "this-week-only" by default, (2) generate next week purely from taste + hard rules, and (3) every Monday ask the user to reconcile what they actually used, then update next week accordingly.
-------------------------------------------
Behavior

1. Pantry semantics





An inventory item is considered "allocated to this week" when added_at <= startOfCurrentWeek (Monday 00:00 local).



A new derived flag (computed in code, no schema change yet — see step 4 for the persisted flag we add) decides whether an item participates in next week's generation. By default: items added on/before the current week start are NOT passed to next-week generation.



Items added after the current week start (mid-week shopping) ARE eligible for next-week generation as normal pantry inputs — those are presumed leftover/extra.

2. Next-week generation

In MaSemaine.tsx > handleGenerate, when launchedWeekStart === nextWeekStart:





Build pantryItems from inventory filtered to items where added_at > thisWeekStart (i.e. only post-Monday additions).



Pass a new boolean useTastePlanningOnly: true in the body.

In supabase/functions/generate-ma-semaine/index.ts:





When useTastePlanningOnly === true:





Skip the "URGENT — prioritize these expiring pantry items" block in the AI prompt (L480 area).



Drop the Pantry: … injected line (or replace with Pantry: (planning by taste only)) and the pantryMatch weighting in the fallback/repair paths.



Keep hard rules untouched: allergies (findAllergenViolations), dietaryPreferences, household size, days/shop/batch schedule, cross-week anchor variety, staples.



Taste preference: continue to read user_taste_profile if already loaded; otherwise add a server-side fetch keyed by user_id (function already has Supabase client) and pass top liked/disliked anchors into the prompt as a soft preference.



"This week" generation keeps current behavior unchanged.

3. Monday reconcile prompt (in-app)

New in-app message delivered via the existing app_notifications + get-inapp-messages flow.





Trigger: first session each Monday (compare last_pantry_reconcile_at profile field — added in step 4 — to current Monday).



UI: new <PantryReconcileSheet /> opened from MaSemaine.tsx and from a banner on /pantry.



Content: lists all inventory items where added_at <= thisWeekStart AND not already reconciled for this week. For each: name, expiry date, quantity.



Actions:





"Mark all as used" (one click) — bulk path.



Per-item toggles: Used / Still have it.



Submit button persists all answers in one round-trip.

4. Reconcile effects

On submit:





Used items → delete from inventory (mirrors how items get consumed elsewhere) and log to consumption_log with source = 'weekly_reconcile'.



Still have it items → set new column inventory.carry_over_week_start = <nextWeekStart> so the next-week generator now treats them as eligible pantry input (overrides the "added before week start" exclusion).



Update profiles.last_pantry_reconcile_at = now().



If any items were marked "still have it": automatically re-invoke generate-ma-semaine for nextWeekStart with useTastePlanningOnly: false, passing the carried-over items as pantryItems (expiring ones still flagged via existing expiring-soon logic, non-expiring as normal pantry). Show toast: "Replanned next week to use leftovers."

Technical details





DB migration (only data/state additions, no destructive change):





ALTER TABLE inventory ADD COLUMN carry_over_week_start date NULL; (indexable, nullable, RLS unaffected — existing policies on inventory already scope by user_id).



ALTER TABLE profiles ADD COLUMN last_pantry_reconcile_at timestamptz NULL;.



Inventory query for next-week generation (client side, no SQL change needed):





eligible = inventory.filter(i => new Date(i.added_at) > thisWeekStart || i.carry_over_week_start === nextWeekStart).



Edge function flag useTastePlanningOnly:





Gates the expiring-priority block, the pantryStr injection, and the pantryMatch scoring weight in supabase/functions/generate-ma-semaine/index.ts.



Fallback paths (buildFallbackDay, deterministic safe pantry bowl) get a parallel branch that uses taste-profile anchors instead of pantryNames.



Monday detection: reuse getCurrentWeekStart() already in MaSemaine.tsx. New helper shouldShowReconcile(profile, now) checks profile.last_pantry_reconcile_at < thisWeekStart.



Reconcile sheet: new file src/components/pantry/PantryReconcileSheet.tsx using existing shadcn Sheet. Mounted in src/pages/MaSemaine.tsx and src/pages/PantryHeatmap.tsx. Localized via existing isFr pattern (EN/FR/ES/DE strings).



In-app message: insert into app_notifications on Monday with kind = 'pantry_reconcile'; the existing notification bell surfaces it. Clicking it opens the same PantryReconcileSheet.



Mutation hook: new usePantryReconcile() in src/hooks/:





delete from inventory for used IDs.



insert into consumption_log for used IDs (best-effort).



update carry_over_week_start = nextWeekStart for kept IDs.



update profiles.last_pantry_reconcile_at.



If any kept → supabase.functions.invoke('generate-ma-semaine', …, weekStart: nextWeekStart).



Tests:





Vitest for eligiblePantryForWeek() helper (empty / mixed / all-old / carry-over cases).



Vitest for shouldShowReconcile() (already-reconciled-this-week, never-reconciled, last-week).



Deno test in supabase/functions/generate-ma-semaine/ confirming useTastePlanningOnly: true removes pantry from the built prompt and still respects allergies/diet.

Out of scope





No change to grocery list, MaSemaine layout, or the "Plan this week" UX.



No change to recipe library or AI provider.



No email/push notification — Monday prompt is in-app only (matches request wording).



Carry-over logic is single-week: items kept this Monday are eligible for next week only; the following Monday's reconcile will re-ask.
